s very important and  they wanted a truly european show with a  mixed cast from different countries this  makes for an interesting setup since  communication problems are built in and  in their words at its heart is the  question of what unites us and what  divides us and how fear can be a trigger  for the latter so what are we looking at  here the official log line from netflix  reads 1899 a migrant steam ship heads  west to leave the old continent the  passengers a mixed bag of european  origins united by their hopes and dreams  for the new century and their future  abroad but their journey takes an  unexpected turn when they discover  another migrant ship a drift on open sea  what they will find on board will turn  their passage to the promised land into  a horrifying nightmare the ship they're  on which you see at the beginning is  called the kerberos and the one that  went missing is the prometheus you learn  that from a newspaper that emily  beatham's character mara franklin is  holding up kerberos is from greek  mythology and is referred to as the  hound of hades it's a multi-headed dog  that guards the gates of the underworld  to prevent the dead from leaving  prometheus is also from myth and is best  known for defying the gods by stealing  fire from them and giving it to humanity  in the form of technology knowledge and  more generally civilization according to  that article the prometheus had been  missing for four months and there's  mention of the devil's triangle or  bermuda triangle under the photo but you  can't really make out the paragraph text  mara looking at herself in the mirror  and saying her name and the date makes  it seem like she might be losing track  of reality or her memories the newspaper  could be a reference point for her it is  the southampton post and she's english  she's got some very noticeable marks on  her wrist that appear to be from  struggling against restraints there's a  quick shot of someone doing just that  that i don't 