 think is a  spark gap transmitter which was a real  thing used to transmit radio waves in  that time period i should mention that  there was a pre-teaser they put out a  week ago where they used morse code to  make the announcement that this trailer  was coming out this week it was a neat  little gimmick and i assumed the images  there were all teasing what we see in  this one but there are quite a few that  aren't included and i've tried to point  those out as they came up  a couple that i haven't mentioned yet  might be on the prometheus after they  discover it you see some of the  passengers and the captain walking  around with lanterns and everything  looks destroyed and deserted there are  also a bunch of creepy looking kids a  couple of which might die or be killed  based on what we see here this trailer  opens with one placing this pyramid on  the carpet from under the table and that  was in a child's hand in the pre-teaser  there's also a shot there where a woman  is holding a candle up to a child's face  and sort of blocking and unblocking the  flame which gives the sense that he's  catatonic or something like that he's  not responding to the flame there's also  a pregnant passenger on board who looks  conflicted in most of the shots that we  see her in as the voiceover tells us  that all of the passengers are running  from something we see her running away  from something literally in the forest  and i do like this idea of characters  being mysterious when we first meet them  and getting to know things about them  through flashbacks that the other  passengers won't be aware of this should  provide fertile ground for speculation  as to why they're making choices and  doing things in the middle of whatever  crisis they find themselves in and there  is a shot of this pregnant woman loading  a shotgun that makes you wonder if she's  looking for revenge the last two shots i  want to talk about are one where someone  is moving their finger towards something  black that appears to be reacting it's a  vague description i know but that's what  you see it almost looks like it's  growing to reach the finger and looks  really otherworldly the other one is  this closing shot where the ship is  being pulled towards this giant  whirlpool it's a fantastic overhead shot  and it looks as though there's lightning  under the waves and i can't wait to see  what's going on here statements like the  passengers are all running from  something and nothing is as it seems  convince me that we're in for a wild  ride and the closing moments you hear  anton lesser's voice say people are  oblivious to reality they only see what  they want to see when all they have to  do is shift their perspective to see the  full scope of things that voice might  sound familiar as kai burns from game of  thrones and his character doesn't show  up in either teaser but we do see him  wearing a jacket with the triangles on  his collar in the behind the scenes  video so perceptions of reality will be  involved we can see that there's going  to be strange happenings on this ship  and they say it will be a visually  stunning odyssey and in that behind the  scenes video they explain more about the  volume technology they use to film it  this is still pretty new and from what  we see in these trailers it all looks  like it came off looking pretty  realistic and i've already talked about  that technology and how it works and  what they built in my last 1899 videos  so i'll just leave a link for that here  for me i'd watch anything the duo behind  dark makes and this looks to be up to my  expectations there's no release date  mentioned yet and i've seen a lot of  guesses that it might be on october 19th  since mara mentions that date in the  teaser dark did release on dates that  were related to its story but as a first  season this state doesn't really have  any importance yet other than it was  mentioned here i've also seen that  someone found the date november 24th in 